{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqi4uvwuwo8","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Process leak: ScheduleWakeup spawns un-reaped detached node setTimeout-sleepers — 187 stale node accumulated over a day","summary":"ROOT CAUSE (diagnosed live 2026-06-17): lib/schedule-wakeup.js implements a scheduled wakeup/task by spawning a DETACHED `node -e` child that just `setTimeout(fire, delaySeconds*1000)` then appends an ORCH_SCHEDULED_TASK marker to a fire file. The daily 'usage reconcile' sleeps 86400000ms (24h). These are NOT de-duplicated or reaped when the same wakeup is re-scheduled, and nothing kills superseded ones — so every heartbeat/loop reschedule + daily task leaves another sleeping node. Observed: 211 node.exe total, 187 from the prior day, only 1 daemon.js (daemon healthy — NOT leaked daemons). Identified by CommandLine on a stale PID. Separately, the bench arms-fix smoke deadlocked 9.5h because its embedded daemon inherited ORCH_HEADLESS_DRAINS=1 and fired its own (hanging) headless drains.\n\nCLEANUP: kill node.exe whose CommandLine matches 'ORCH_SCHEDULED_TASK' (precise; spares daemon.js / Adobe / Claude desktop).\n\nPREVENTION (the durable fix): (1) schedule-wakeup.js must DEDUP + REAP — track spawned wakeup PIDs in a registry file; on re-schedule of the same logical wakeup, kill the prior sleeper before spawning; reap on fire/cancel. (2) Add a GC reaper (scripts/gc-stale-spawns.js + daemon-boot hook, mirroring gc-worktrees.js / gc-filedrop-stubs.js) that kills orphaned ORCH_SCHEDULED_TASK + stale subagent node processes older than a max-lifetime. (3) BOUND every spawned child with a hard timeout (the 9.5h smoke had none). (4) Spawn the embedded bench daemon with ORCH_HEADLESS_DRAINS=0 (the autonomous drains hang + leak; use manual node-scoped drains). (5) Consider turning ORCH_HEADLESS_DRAINS off globally until the hang/auth is fixed.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-17T13:55:01.518Z","vec":[-0.10282803326845169,0.052406664937734604,0.0194912608712